---
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: Astro uses this layout component below.
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="FAQ | plansplease"
  description="Answers about the plansplease CLI, cloud workspace, privacy, and alpha plans."
  activePath="faq"
>
  <section class="faq-hero" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <div class="faq-hero-content">
      <h1 id="faq-title">Questions we expect to hear.</h1>
      <p class="faq-lead">
        Clear, direct answers about how plansplease handles local loopback serving, private cloud
        vaults, and agent integrations.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="faq-content">
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item" open>
        <summary>
          <span>What is plansplease?</span>
          <span class="faq-toggle-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            plansplease gives agent-generated web artifacts a permanent, interactive home. Coding
            agents (Claude, Cursor, ChatGPT, Gemini) often output complete single-page tools,
            simulators, or dashboards.
          </p>
          <p>
            The plansplease CLI creates an instant, zero-latency local preview on your machine,
            while our cloud workspace securely archives your pages so they never get lost in a
            closed chat thread.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span>What file types and assets can I preview?</span>
          <span class="faq-toggle-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            The local CLI serves both standalone HTML files and multi-file directory bundles with an
            <code>index.html</code> entry point. You can include linked stylesheets, images, client-side
            JavaScript, Canvas scripts, and CDN-hosted libraries (like Tailwind, Chart.js, or React).
          </p>
          <p>
            The cloud workspace currently accepts standalone HTML files with full support for inline
            scripts and CDN dependencies.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span>Why not just open the HTML file with my browser?</span>
          <span class="faq-toggle-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            Modern browsers enforce strict security restrictions on <code>file://</code> URLs. They
            block CORS requests, break relative asset fetching, prevent web workers from loading, and
            restrict Canvas manipulation.
          </p>
          <p>
            plansplease runs a minimal loopback daemon on <code>127.0.0.1</code> that serves your
            files over genuine HTTP, eliminating all sandboxing errors with zero configuration.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span>How does plansplease connect with Claude Code or Cursor?</span>
          <span class="faq-toggle-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            You can use the plansplease CLI directly inside your agent's terminal shell, or configure
            plansplease as an MCP (Model Context Protocol) tool. This allows your agent to publish
            and inspect live interactive artifacts autonomously during its planning and coding loop.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span>Is my data private and secure?</span>
          <span class="faq-toggle-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            Yes. The local CLI serves strictly over your machine's private loopback interface—none of
            your local code or data is transmitted externally. In the cloud workspace, all uploads
            are secured behind GitHub OAuth authentication and tied to your personal account.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span>Is plansplease open source?</span>
          <span class="faq-toggle-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            Yes! The entire core runtime, CLI, local daemon, and storage engine are 100% open source
            under an permissive license on
            <a href="https://github.com/abijith-suresh/planview">GitHub</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>

    <p class="page-note">
      Have a question that is not covered here? Open an issue on
      <a href="https://github.com/abijith-suresh/planview">GitHub</a> or visit the
      <a href="../docs/">documentation page</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .faq-hero {
    padding: clamp(3.5rem, 6vh, 5rem) 0 2.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--night-border);
  }

  .faq-hero-content {
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .faq-hero h1 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--text-white);
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 3.8vw, 3.2rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .faq-lead {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--night-muted);
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.3vw, 1.15rem);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .faq-content {
    padding: 3.5rem 0 5rem;
  }

  .faq-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .faq-item {
    border: 1px solid var(--night-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--night-card);
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: border-color 160ms ease;
  }

  .faq-item:hover,
  .faq-item[open] {
    border-color: var(--night-border-hover);
  }

  .faq-item summary {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem;
    color: var(--text-white);
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    cursor: pointer;
    user-select: none;
  }

  .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-toggle-icon {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--mint);
    transition: transform 180ms ease;
  }

  .faq-item[open] .faq-toggle-icon {
    transform: rotate(45deg);
  }

  .faq-answer {
    padding: 0 1.75rem 1.75rem;
    color: var(--night-muted);
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--night-border);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .faq-answer p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .faq-answer p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .faq-answer code {
    padding: 0.15rem 0.35rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: var(--night-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--night-border);
    color: var(--mint);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .faq-answer a,
  .page-note a {
    color: var(--mint);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
</style>
